## Machine information tabs
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_thermal_crusher=Crushes supported materials into processed resources. Each completed cycle consumes §sDorios Energy§8 and produces the configured result. Heat rises after processing and falls while idle.\n\n§8Slots:\n- §9Input§8: material to crush.\n- §cOutput§8: processed result.\n\n§8Accepted Upgrades:\n- §dSpeed§8: increases processing speed and energy cost.\n- §dEfficiency§8: reduces effective energy consumption.\n- §dBatch§8: processes additional crafts together.\n- §dThermal§8: increases heat capacity and cooling.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_infuser=Combines a base item with a catalyst while consuming §sDorios Energy§8. Each combination defines its required quantities, output amount and processing cost.\n\n§8Slots:\n- §9Base Input§8: the primary material.\n- §bCatalyst Input§8: the second ingredient.\n- §cOutput§8: infused result.\n\n§8Accepted Upgrades:\n- §dSpeed§8, §dEfficiency§8 and §dBatch§8.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_fluid_washer=Processes an item while consuming 250 mB of §gExample Coolant§8 per craft and §sDorios Energy§8. The liquid tank must contain Example Coolant.\n\n§8Slots and resources:\n- §9Item Input§8: material to wash.\n- §cItem Output§8: washed result.\n- §gCoolant Tank§8: liquid consumed by recipes.\n\n§8Accepted Upgrades:\n- §dSpeed§8, §dEfficiency§8 and §dBatch§8.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_gas_reactor=Consumes an iron catalyst and §uExample Hydrogen§8 to create crystal shards and §uExample Exhaust§8. Both gas tanks have fixed types, so input and output gases remain compatible with automation.\n\n§8Slots and resources:\n- §9Catalyst Input§8: iron ingots.\n- §cItem Output§8: crystal shards.\n- §uHydrogen Tank§8: gas input.\n- §uExhaust Tank§8: gas output.\n\n§8Accepted Upgrades:\n- §dSpeed§8, §dEfficiency§8 and §dBatch§8.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_solar_generator=Generates §sDorios Energy§8 during daytime while the block above it is air. It pauses at night, under a solid block or when its energy storage is full. It needs no item, liquid or gas IO.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_biofuel_generator=Consumes §gExample Biofuel§8 to generate §sDorios Energy§8. Each liquid unit provides 30 DE, and generation pauses when the tank is empty or energy storage is full.\n\n§8Resources:\n- §vBiofuel Input§8: liquid fuel accepted through configured faces.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_gas_turbine=Consumes §uExample Hydrogen§8 to generate §sDorios Energy§8. Each gas unit provides 40 DE, and generation pauses when the gas tank is empty or energy storage is full.\n\n§8Resources:\n- §vHydrogen Input§8: gas fuel accepted through configured faces.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_factory_crusher=This controller activates a Heavy Machinery-style multiblock. Energy cells determine capacity, processing modules determine batch size, and speed or efficiency modules modify runtime statistics.\n\n§8Controller slots:\n- §9Material Input§8.\n- §cProduct Output§8.\n\nExternal item and energy ports expose multiblock IO; they are configured on the port blocks rather than in this controller screen.
ui.utilitycraft:info.example_biofuel_dynamo=This controller activates a liquid-fueled multiblock generator. Energy cells determine energy capacity and liquid cells determine §gExample Biofuel§8 capacity.\n\nExternal liquid and energy ports expose multiblock IO; they are configured on the port blocks rather than in this controller screen.

